C. Participants
The eight experts who participated in this heuristic evaluation were all technical engineers (4) and interface designers (4) responsible for AR-HUD development. Their average working age is 5.88 (SD=1.553).
IV. TEST RESULTS AND ANALYSIS
After usability testing, we obtained interview text and questionnaire score data. Subsequently, we used IBM SPSS 26.0 statistical software to conduct a one-way repeated measures ANOVA analysis of the questionnaire score.
A. Heuristic evaluation results
In the heuristic evaluation, each expert evaluated the ARHUD of each car in three dimensions. In the dimension of the function, compared with VW ID.6 and EXEED RX, the Benz EQS lacks snow functions. In addition, VW ID.6 and EXEED RX are more flexible in HUD settings. The HUDs of these two cars can independently cancel information such as navigation, assisted driving, and traffic signs. However, Benz EQS has 5 HUD modes: minimalist, sports, standard, AR, and energy-saving. In addition, the Benz EQS automatically detects the driver's head position and instantly adjusts the AR display position on the HUD.
In the visual dimension, experts agree that the Benz ESQ’s AR-HUD is clearer and more transparent than the other two cars. The clarity of the VW ID.6's AR navigation display is the worst, and the AR navigation arrows cannot even be seen under strong light and special backgrounds. In addition, some icons and text in the AR-HUD interfaces of Benz ESQ and VW ID.6 are too small and difficult to read. The AR navigation instructions of EXEED RX could be better. Because its AR indication is different from that of an actual road situation, and the AR arrow is too small. In the emotional dimension, the Benz ESQ captivated participants with its outstanding dynamic effect design. Therefore, Benz ESQ is also the best in terms of satisfaction.
B. Questionnaire Results
According to the one-way repeated measures ANOVA on the six facets of the questionnaire in TABLE III, willingness to use (F2,14=13.267, P=0.000 ＜ 0.05), sense of experience (F2,14=12.629, P=0.000 ＜ 0.05), sense of security (F2,14=6.635, P=0.009 ＜ 0.05) and aesthetics (F2,14=25.282, P=0.000＜0.05) have significant main effects.

