Regarding the willingness to use AR-HUD, the Post Hoc test (LSD) results show that there is a significant difference between Benz EQS (M=4.75, SD=0.463) and VW ID.6X (M=2.88, SD=0.991) (P=0.002 <0.05). There is also a significant difference between Benz EQS and EXEED RX (M=3.13, SD=1.246) (P=0.006<0.05). In the facet of ARHUD experience, there is a significant difference between Benz EQS (M=4.75, SD=0.463) and VW ID.6X (M=3.50, SD=0.756) (P=0.011<0.05). There is also a significant difference between Benz EQS and EXEED RX (M=2.88, SD=0.835) (P=0.000＜0.05). Regarding the sense of security of AR-HUD, there is a significant difference between Benz EQS (M=4.13, SD=0.835) and EXEED RX (M=2.63, SD=0.916) (P=0.003<0.05). In the facet of the aesthetics of AR-HUD, there is a significant difference between Benz EQS (M=4.63, SD=0.518) and VW ID.6X (M=2.38, SD=0.744) (P=0.000<0.05). There is also a significant difference between Benz EQS and EXEED RX (M=2.50, SD=0.926) (P=0.000<0.05). In other words, Benz EQS’s AR-HUD is the best choice in terms of willingness to use, sense of experience, sense of security, and aesthetics.
V. CONCLUSION
From interviews with experts, we learned that the current AR-HUD has too much information in the interface, which may interfere with the driver's attention to the surrounding environment [6]. While the performance of the Benz EQS in our evaluation is commendable, the usability issues we listed in our heuristic evaluation also need to be considered. The reason why Benz EQS's AR-HUD performs better may be due to the application of Digital Light Processing (DLP) imaging technology on the one hand. On the other hand, more cool and interesting dynamic effects were added to its interface design (see Fig. 2). Benz EQS displays impactful indication effects on both the HUD and the central control screen during AR navigation. The AR-HUD of the other two models is stiffer and more mediocre in visual effects.
